Local compatibility patch for the pinned WIMpy install (NOT upstream).

Target:    bradkav/WIMpy_NREFT @ 50581c637069305a3def3865462ef1b4ed9a616d, file WIMpy/DMUtils.py
Applies to: .venv-sidm-bench/Lib/site-packages/WIMpy/DMUtils.py -- the venv that
            scripts/verify_release_gate.py runs on (its VENV_PYTHON, line 64).
Why:       upstream imports scipy.integrate.trapz and scipy.integrate.cumtrapz. SciPy 1.18
           removed both names (trapezoid / cumulative_trapezoid). Against this repo's own pins
           (scipy 1.18.1) an unpatched WIMpy import fails, and Channel 26
           (loglike_lz_magnetic_moment) then returns 0 by design -- a physics channel switched
           off by an import error, with its 36 assertions deselected rather than failing.
Found:     2026-11-04, by diffing the installed file against the pinned upstream commit fetched
           from raw.githubusercontent.com. Installed sha256 199065ab55244a8a..., upstream sha256
           7b9f1ae8a729fe4f...; the whole difference is 3 added / 1 removed lines. Generated
           from that diff so a fresh host can rebuild the same environment instead of inheriting
           an unrecorded hand edit.
Apply:     cd <the .venv-sidm-bench site-packages dir>
           patch -p1 < .../v0.3-prelim/patches/0003-wimpy-scipy118-trapezoid.patch
Verify:    python -c "import WIMpy; print('WIMpy ok')"
Verified:    applied to a pristine copy of the pinned upstream file -> byte-identical to the
           installed file after normalising line endings (installed file is CRLF, 927 CRs; the
           patch produces LF). Verified with patch -p1 --dry-run and sha256 on 2026-11-04.
Status:    third-party local edit, not upstream, not submitted upstream. Re-apply after any
           WIMpy reinstall or Channel 26 dies silently.

